// v0.9.3

// Added
- 'find': Add support for globbing with ? (single element) and * (one or
  more elements).
  e.g., 'find x:FF ? FF' finds the next entry to [ 0xff, ?, 0xff ].
- '0o' as a pattern alias to 'o:', the octal prefix.
- 'goto' command now understands the binary sequence with the 0b prefix.
- TIOCGWINSZ definition for OpenBSD.
- Readline also allows Escape to cancel input.

// Fixed
- Respect VINTR (c_cc[VINTR] on POSIX platforms) and AsciiChar == \003 on
  Windows for ^C (EXT), instead of hardcoding the Ctrl+C check.
  - Previous versions hardcoded the ^C check to Ctrl+C to cancel actions,
    which may be different in other keyboard layouts.
  - We're talking possibly Dvorak, Colemak, Workman, Neo, BEPO, YCUKEH...
- Readline no longer shouts "Cancelled" when cancelling input.

