// v0.9.2

Small update with status bar customization and fixes.

// Status Customization

Three configurable format strings: 'status-format', 'status-selection',
'status-report'.

Bars:
- 'status-format': The regular status bar.
  - Defaults to "%e %m | %t | %c | %8p"
- 'status-selection': Status bar when there is an active selection.
  - Defaults to "SEL: %V (%v Bytes)"
- 'status-report': Status message for the 'report' (Ctrl+P) command.
  - Defaults to "%d / %s B (%q%%)"

Specifiers:
  %f     Target file basename
  %F     Full target path
  %s     Document size in bytes (decimal)
  %S     Document size in human-readable format (B, K, M, G, T, P)
  %P     Document size in current address format
  %p     Cursor position in current address format
  %d     Cursor position in decimal
  %h     Cursor position in hexadecimal
  %o     Cursor position in octal
  %q     Cursor position as percentage
  %v     Selection length in bytes
  %V     Selection range in current address format
  %e     Edited indicator (* or space)
  %m     Writing mode (OVR, INS, DIG, R/O)
  %c     Character set
  %t     Data type
  %%     Literal %

// Width and Alignment

An optional width can be added between '%' and the specifier.

- '%10p' -- right-align in 10-character field.
- '%-20f' -- left-align in 20-character field.
- No padding added if the result is already wider than the specified
  width.

// Added
- Status bar customization!
  - 'status-format', 'status-selection', 'status-report' configurations.
  - Printf-like specifiers with support for width.
- Other possible values for "data" configuration, only affects
  --help-config.
- TIOCGWINSZ definition for NetBSD. ddhx works on NetBSD!

// Changed
- Improved readline function that accepts accents on Windows and POSIX
  platforms.
  - On Windows, wide characters are translated to CP_UTF8 to match output
    codepage.
  - On POSIX, input filtering was improved.
- Renamed 'report-position' command to 'report'.
  - The command was repurposed to perform just a form of customized user
    report.

// Fixed
- Fix when turning off status bar would cause visual glitches.
- Fix selection in an empty file (zero-length) causing overflow.
- Fix "bind" command parameters in interactive mode.
- Fix capturing ctrl+return on POSIX platforms.

